# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Remote Backend Configuration Examples
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The local backend (default in provider.tf) does NOT support state locking.
# For production deployments with multiple collaborators or CI/CD pipelines,
# use one of the remote backends below.
#
# Prerequisites for any remote backend:
# 1. Create the storage bucket/container before running `tofu init`
# 2. Ensure credentials are available (env vars, service account, or IAM role)
# 3. Run `tofu init -migrate-state` to move existing state from local to remote

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Option 1: AWS S3 with DynamoDB Locking (Recommended)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Requires:
#   - An S3 bucket (e.g. homelab-tfstate-<account-id>)
#   - A DynamoDB table for locking (e.g. homelab-tfstate-lock)
#     Partition key: LockID (String)
#   - AWS credentials via env vars or ~/.aws/credentials
#
# Create resources manually or with:
#   aws s3 mb s3://homelab-tfstate-123456789 --region us-east-1
#   aws dynamodb create-table \
#     --table-name homelab-tfstate-lock \
#     --attribute-definitions AttributeName=LockID,AttributeType=S \
#     --key-schema AttributeName=LockID,KeyType=HASH \
#     --billing-mode PAY_PER_REQUEST \
#     --region us-east-1

# Uncomment and place in provider.tf (replace the backend "local" block):
#
# backend "s3" {
#   bucket         = "homelab-tfstate-123456789"
#   key            = "homelab/terraform.tfstate"
#   region         = "us-east-1"
#   dynamodb_table = "homelab-tfstate-lock"
#   encrypt        = true
# }

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Option 2: Google Cloud Storage (GCS)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Requires:
#   - A GCS bucket (e.g. homelab-tfstate-<project-id>)
#   - GCP credentials via GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS or gcloud auth
#   - Object versioning enabled on the bucket (provides locking)
#
# Create the bucket:
#   gsutil mb gs://homelab-tfstate-myproject
#   gsutil versioning set on gs://homelab-tfstate-myproject

# Uncomment and place in provider.tf (replace the backend "local" block):
#
# backend "gcs" {
#   bucket = "homelab-tfstate-myproject"
#   prefix = "homelab"
# }

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Option 3: Azure Storage
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Requires:
#   - An Azure Storage Account and Blob Container
#   - Azure credentials via AZURE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT / AZURE_STORAGE_KEY or az login
#   - Leases enabled on the container (default for Azure Blob, provides locking)

# Uncomment and place in provider.tf (replace the backend "local" block):
#
# backend "azurerm" {
#   resource_group_name  = "homelab-rg"
#   storage_account_name = "homelabtfstate"
#   container_name       = "tfstate"
#   key                  = "homelab/terraform.tfstate"
# }

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Option 4: Terraform Cloud / HCP Terraform
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Requires:
#   - A Terraform Cloud account and organization
#   - A workspace (e.g. homelab)
#   - TERRAFORM_CLOUD_TOKEN env var or ~/.terraform.d/credentials.tfrc.json

# Uncomment and place in provider.tf (replace the backend "local" block):
#
# cloud {
#   organization = "my-org"
#   workspaces {
#     name = "homelab"
#   }
# }

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Migration Steps
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. Choose a backend from the options above
# 2. Create the required cloud resources (bucket, table, etc.)
# 3. Replace the `backend "local"` block in provider.tf with your chosen backend
# 4. Run: tofu init -migrate-state
# 5. Confirm the migration when prompted
# 6. Verify: tofu plan (should show no changes)
